<fcntl.h> gives the file mode constants, as POSIX has it.

POSIX: "The <fcntl.h> header shall define the symbolic constants for
file modes for use as values of mode_t as described in <sys/stat.h>"
-- S_IRUSR and the rest, which open(path, O_CREAT, S_IRUSR | S_IWUSR)
needs and which a program reasonably expects from the header that
declares open(). glibc and musl both provide them there; picolibc did
not, and procps-ng's watch stopped on S_IRUSR undeclared. The whole of
<sys/stat.h> comes with them, as on glibc.

--- a/libc/include/fcntl.h
+++ b/libc/include/fcntl.h
@@ -31,3 +31,4 @@
 SUCH DAMAGE.
  */
 #include <sys/fcntl.h>
+#include <sys/stat.h>
